evidence.quote:
This extinction-corrected H$\alpha$ flux is converted to a SFR using the relation of (cite: kennicutt2012star): $$\begin{equation}
  \log({\rm SFR}\,/\,{\rm M}_\odot\,{\rm yr}^{-1})=\log(L_{\rm H\alpha}\,/\,{\rm ergs}\,{\rm s}^{-1})-41.27~,
\end{equation}$$

The complete conversion thus becomes $$\begin{equation}
  \frac{M_{\rm H_2}}{{\rm M}_\odot}=6.325\,\left(\frac{L_{\rm CO(2-1)}}{\rm K~km~s^{-1}~pc^2}\right).
\end{equation}$$ The molecular gas mass surface density is then calculated as $M_{\rm H_2}$ divided by the spaxel area.
